---
components: ["ImageViewer"]
description: Image viewers show one image in a frame that zooms and pans, for product photos, diagrams, and screenshots that need a closer look.
---

<script>
  import { Box, ImageViewer, Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Set `src` and `alt`. The image fits the frame, and the frame is a focusable image region that announces `alt`.

Zoom with the buttons, the mouse wheel while holding <DocKbd label="Ctrl" />, a trackpad pinch, or a touch pinch. Each zoom keeps the point under the cursor or between the fingers still. Drag a zoomed image to pan it; it coasts a little after release and stops at the edges. Double-click or double-tap to switch between fit and 100%.

With the frame focused, <DocKbd label="+" /> and <DocKbd label="-" /> zoom, <DocKbd label="0" /> fits the image, <DocKbd label="Enter" /> switches between fit and 100%, and the arrow keys pan a zoomed image. A live region announces the zoom level once it settles.

With reduced motion requested, a pan does not coast and a zoom does not animate.

<ImageViewer
  ratio="4x3"
  src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg/1280px-The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg"
  alt="Photograph of Earth taken by the Apollo 17 crew"
/>

## Usage

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Write `alt` for what the image shows. | It names the region, and it is the only description a screen reader user gets of the image. |
| Pass `width` and `height` when you know them. | The viewer lays the image out before it loads, so the frame does not shift. |
| Use it where detail matters, such as a diagram or a screenshot. | A picture people only glance at needs no zoom controls. |
| Open the image in a [Lightbox](/components/Lightbox) when there is little room inline. | A small frame limits how much of a zoomed image shows at once. |
| Serve an image that is at most a few thousand pixels wide, and a smaller one for the page. | The browser holds the whole decoded image once it is zoomed in: about 190 MB for 8000 by 6000. |

## Zoom

### Bind the zoom

Bind `zoom` to read or set it. `"fit"` shows the whole image, and a number is a scale where 1 is 100%. A zoom within a hair of fit snaps back to `"fit"`, and `zoomed` is `true` while the image is zoomed in.

<FileSource src="/framed/ImageViewer/ImageViewerZoom" />

### Maximum zoom

Set `maxZoom` to limit how far in a user can go. The default is 4, or 400%. The limit is never below the fit scale.

<ImageViewer
  ratio="16x9"
  maxZoom={1}
  src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/1280px-FullMoon2010.jpg"
  alt="The full Moon"
/>

## Mouse wheel

By default only <DocKbd label="Ctrl" /> and the wheel zoom, so the page keeps scrolling while the pointer is over an inline viewer. A plain wheel pans a zoomed image. Set `wheel` to `"always"` for a viewer that fills the window, where every wheel event zooms.

<Stack gap={6}>
  <ImageViewer
    ratio="16x9"
    src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Saturn_during_Equinox.jpg/1280px-Saturn_during_Equinox.jpg"
    alt="Saturn at equinox"
  />
  <ImageViewer
    wheel="always"
    ratio="16x9"
    src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Mars_Valles_Marineris.jpeg/1280px-Mars_Valles_Marineris.jpeg"
    alt="Valles Marineris on Mars"
  />
</Stack>

## Frame

### Aspect ratio

Set `ratio` to give the frame an [AspectRatio](/components/AspectRatio). It takes the same values.

<ImageViewer
  ratio="1x1"
  src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Saturn_during_Equinox.jpg/1280px-Saturn_during_Equinox.jpg"
  alt="Saturn at equinox"
/>

### Fill the parent

Without `ratio`, the frame fills the height of its parent, with a minimum height. Give the parent a height, as a viewer in a panel or a window has.

<Box height="20rem">
  <ImageViewer
    src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Mars_Valles_Marineris.jpeg/1280px-Mars_Valles_Marineris.jpeg"
    alt="Valles Marineris on Mars"
  />
</Box>

### Controls

Set `controls` to `false` to hide the zoom buttons. Gestures and keys still work, and the `zoomIn()`, `zoomOut()`, `zoomTo(scale)`, `toggle()`, `reset()` and `pan(dx, dy)` methods are there to build your own.

<ImageViewer
  controls={false}
  ratio="16x9"
  src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/FullMoon2010.jpg/1280px-FullMoon2010.jpg"
  alt="The full Moon"
/>

## Loading and errors

While the image loads, the viewer shows a skeleton. If it fails, the viewer shows a message and a retry button, and the frame stops being an image region so the button can be reached. Replace either with the `loading` and `error` slots, as in [ImageLoader](/components/ImageLoader). The `error` slot gets a `retry` function.

<ImageViewer
  ratio="16x9"
  src="https://example.invalid/missing.jpg"
  alt="Quarterly capacity report"
  errorText="The report image is unavailable."
/>

## Right to left

The image keeps its own left and right in a right-to-left page, so a pan or a zoom follows the pointer the same way. The controls move to the inline end of the frame.

<div dir="rtl">
  <ImageViewer
    ratio="16x9"
    src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg/1280px-The_Earth_seen_from_Apollo_17.jpg"
    alt="Photograph of Earth taken by the Apollo 17 crew"
  />
</div>
